~ start
Wendy: Where are you, Danilo...
Wendy: I tried calling him, but he didn’t answer.
Wendy: Should I go back too?
Wendy: He should’ve been home already... it’s been a day.
Wendy: I’m worried... I should probably go back.
Wendy: Just to check if he’s alright.
do Hud.show_objectives()
=> END

~ hometown
do ObjectiveManager.complete_objective(1)
Wendy: It’s been a while since I came back here.
Wendy: I just hope Danilo’s fine.
Wendy: Maybe I’ll go... I’ll try surprising Lola first.
do Hud.show_objectives()
=> END

~ notice
do ObjectiveManager.complete_objective(2)
Wendy: Umm...
Wendy: Why are there so many people outside?
Wendy: What’s going on?
=> END

~ lola_spotted
Wendy: Lola is outside.
Wendy: Is she waiting for someone?
Wendy: I haven’t told her I’m coming home yet.
=> END

~ talk_to_lola_ising
do ObjectiveManager.complete_objective(3)
Wendy: Oh, Lola, why are you outside?
Wendy: Did you expect me to come home?
Wendy: I also brought you a gift.
Lola Ising: Later, apo...
Lola Ising: There’s something more important you need to know...
Lola Ising: Apo... apo... it's about Danilo...
Wendy: What happened to Danilo, Lola?
Lola Ising: He’s missing...
Wendy: What do you mean missing, Lola? 
Lola Ising: I saw him leave the house last night.
Lola Ising: I thought he was with someone, so I let him go.
Lola Ising: But the next day...
Lola Ising: He didn’t come back home.
Wendy: Have you already looked for him?
Lola Ising: Yes, we’ve been searching since yesterday... but still no sign.
Wendy: Where could Danilo be?
Wendy: Okay, Lola.
Wendy: I’ll try gathering some information.
Wendy: Maybe that way, we can get some clues on where he is now.
=> END

~ talk_to_jonathan
Wendy: Hello, Jonathan.
Jonathan: Oh, Wendy, you’re home too.
Jonathan: Did you know Danilo is missing?
Jonathan: Just the other day I spoke to him briefly.
Jonathan: Then he disappeared like a wisp of smoke... we couldn’t find him.
Wendy: You talked to Danilo before he disappeared?
Jonathan: Yes, we were going home together, but he didn’t seem to notice me.
Jonathan: I was about to approach him...
Jonathan: Then suddenly he ran off.
Wendy: Do you know why he ran?
Jonathan: I don’t... I only saw him again the next day.
Wendy: What were you talking about back then?
Jonathan: He was just asking some questions at the time.
Wendy: Hmm... I see. Did you notice anything unusual about him?
Jonathan: Nothing obvious, but he seemed a little... [wave amp=25 freq=5]alert[/wave].
Wendy: Ok, thank you, Jonathan.
=> END

~ talk_to_vanesa
Wendy: Hello, Vanesa. It’s been a while.
Vanesa: Oh, hello, Wendy.
Vanesa: You haven’t changed at all.
Wendy: I’m curious... did you talk to or see Danilo before he disappeared?
Vanesa: Oh, yes.
Vanesa: I remember he asked if I had seen anyone following him on his way home.
Vanesa: At that time, I didn’t know he came here.
Vanesa: He only asked and came to the house briefly.
Wendy: Did you see anyone following him?
Vanesa: No, I was inside doing laundry... didn’t notice anyone.
Vanesa: Maybe if I had been out hanging clothes, I could’ve seen something.
Wendy: Ah, I see. Thank you for the info, Vanesa.
=> END

~ talk_to_manang_matet
Wendy: Hello, Tita Matet.
Manang Matet: Oh, apo, you’re here.
Manang Matet: Did you hear that Danilo is missing?
Wendy: Yes, I just heard it from Lola.
Manang Matet: Wow... I haven’t even checked on him.
Manang Matet: Jonathan said he knocked at the house a few days ago.
Manang Matet: But I was at the hospital at that time.
Manang Matet: I thought he’d come the next day to check on me.
Manang Matet: But he didn’t, so I went to them instead.
Manang Matet: I even cooked his favorite dish.
Manang Matet: I hope we find him soon.
Wendy: I’ll help look for him.
Wendy: You should rest now.
Manang Matet: Thank you, apo.
=> END

~ talk_to_mang_gino
Wendy: Hello, Mang Gino.
Mang Gino: If this is about Danilo, I haven’t spoken to him.
Wendy: Ah, I see. Thank you.
=> END

~ talk_to_aling_theresa
Wendy: Hello, Aling Theresa.
Wendy: I want to ask if you saw or spoke to Danilo before he disappeared.
Aling Theresa: Oh, yes, he asked me something, but I didn’t fully understand.
Aling Theresa: My hearing and eyesight aren’t that good anymore.
Aling Theresa: But I didn’t see him.
Wendy: Thank you, Aling Theresa.
Wendy: Walang anuman, apo.
=> END

~ wendy_contemplate
Wendy: [center]From everyone I asked...[/center]
Wendy: [center]I think Danilo is troubled by something, but...[/center]
Wendy: [center]During our calls, he seemed normal.[/center]
Wendy: [center]I need to find him quickly. He needs his meds already.[/center]
=> END

~ signage1
Wendy: The playground... this is where we used to play.
=> END

~ lola_final
Wendy: Okay, Lola, I’ll go ahead first.
Wendy: You should rest now.
Wendy: Please tell everyone to rest as well.
Lola Ising: Ok, apo. We’ll follow once we finish resting.
Wendy: Thank you, Lola. I’ll go ahead.
=> END

~ lola_here
Lola Ising: I’ll stay here for now, apo.
Lola Ising: Talk to the neighbors first.
=> END

~ wendy_start
Wendy: So, what places have you all checked already?
Aling Theresa: Including the neighboring village... they’ve been searching there too.
Vanesa: Kapitan has also been searching in town... still no sign.
Lola Ising: We found the playground where you used to play, which we had forbidden you to go before.
Manang Matet: We also went to the places Mateo used to hide when you were kids.
Wendy: What do you mean by hiding, Tita?
Manang Matet: Oh, you didn’t know.
Manang Matet: Mateo liked hiding back then... sometimes he wouldn’t come home and would sleep elsewhere.
Manang Matet: He preferred that over hearing everyone fight.
Wendy: Tita...
Wendy: I didn’t know Mateo had places like that.
Wendy: Don’t lose hope. We’ll find Mateo... 
Wendy: And now, Danilo too.
=> END

~ mang_gino_Cliff_hint
Mang Gino: Wait...
Wendy: What is it, Mang Gino?
Mang Gino: ...
Wendy: Sorry, but I need to find Danilo.
Mang Gino: ...
Mang Gino: I know a place you haven’t gone yet.
Manang Matet: Why didn’t you say that sooner?
Mang Gino: That part is thick with vegetation... hard to reach.
Mang Gino: But I cleared a path, so we can cross.
Mang Gino: The path is near the cliff... only a few know it.
Wendy: I see...
Wendy: Thanks, Mang Gino.
Wendy: Let’s go there first.
=> END

~ enter_dark_forest
Wendy: [center]Wait for me, Danilo... We won’t give up finding you.[/center]
=> END

~ signage_darkforest
Wendy: Based on this sign... Mang Gino, is this the right upward path?
Mang Gino: Yes... that’s the one we’ll take.
=> END

~ cliff_entry
Mang Gino: Be careful, everyone. Remember, we’re walking along a cliff.
Wendy: [center]...[/center]
Wendy: [center]Please... Danilo, I hope you’re here.[/center]
=> END

~ seen_danilo
Wendy: [shake]Danilo!!![/shake]
Wendy: [shake]What happened to you?![/shake]
Wendy: [shake]Please, wake up![/shake]
Wendy: [shake]Danilo!!![/shake]
=> END
